We have derived improved differentiability properties for solutions to a non-autonomous obstacle problem, formulated as
  \begin{equation*}
  \min\left\{\int_{\Omega}f\left(x, Dv(x)\right)dx, v\geq \psi\text{ in } \Omega, v\geq w\text{ in } \Omega\right\}.
  \end{equation*}
  Here, the data function $f$ exhibits sub-quadratic growth with respect to the gradient argument and the given obstacles $\psi$ and $w$ depend only on the domain variable. With a given differentiability rate for the optimal solution, we have a sub-quadratic differentiability rate for the optimal solution. With additional assumptions, we have obtained an autonomy-based regularity result and a boundedness result with respect to the given data function $f$. The sub-quadratic nature of this problem distinguishes it from previously studied problems.
